.TH BYTE_FMT 3
.SH NAME
byte_fmt \- format a byte array using a custom formatter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <byte.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t byte_fmt(const char* " in ", size_t " in_len ", stralloc* " out ", size_t (*" fmt_function ")(char*, unsigned int ch));"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B byte_fmt
transforms an input byte array
.I in
of length
.I in_len
into a formatted representation, appending the result to the
.B stralloc
structure
.IR out .
.PP
The function iterates over each byte in
.I in
and invokes the provided
.I fmt_function
callback for every byte. The callback is expected to write the formatted representation of the byte into the provided character buffer and return the number of bytes written.
.PP
The
.I out
stralloc is cleared before the formatting process begins, and its length is adjusted to match the final size of the formatted output.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the total number of bytes appended to
.IR out ,
or 0 if an internal memory allocation failure occurred.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stralloc (3)